title: The Second War at the Top

# Wojna na górze II. The first war at the top was Wałęsa against Mazowiecki in
# 1990. The reference for this one is Kwaśniewski against Miller in 2003–04:
# one camp holds the Palace and the cabinet, the president polls far above a
# sinking prime minister, and the presidency becomes the instrument for
# replacing him. Eligibility, camp identity and pair heat are computed monthly
# in poland_normalize; the stages here only move the bloc and the settlement.
#
# Entry points: the June 2026 Tribunal ruling (poland_events_2026,
# @tribunal_competence_2026) for any camp, and a May 2024 opener for a KO
# cabinet under a President Trzaskowski elected in 2020. Later stages are gated
# on elapsed months, not on calendar dates, so both entries use one chain.


@war_top_open_ko
# prose-audit: Grade B — The early KO entry names both officeholders, the
# restoration they are fighting over and Lewica's real position inside the
# cabinet; each response trades ownership of the repair against the Palace
# relationship rather than a generic loyalty score.
title: The President and the Prime Minister claim the same restoration
subtitle: One camp holds the Palace and the cabinet, and only one of them can own the repair
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace-interior.webp
new-page: true
