on-arrival: {!
Q.war_top_stage = 1;
Q.war_top_camp = Q.war_top_camp_live;
Q.war_top_heat = Q.war_top_heat_live;
Q.war_top_started_time = Number(Q.time) || 0;
Q.war_top_president = String(Q.president_name || "");
Q.war_top_pm = String(Q.prime_minister || "");
Q.war_top_origin = "ko_2024";
Q.war_top_palace_bloc = 20;
Q.news_headline =
    "Commentators call the Palace–Chancellery quarrel a second war at the top";
!}

= May 2024 — Two offices, one camp, one restoration

**[+ war_top_president +]** has held the Palace since 2020. **[+ war_top_pm +]**
has held the Chancellery since the coalition took office. They belong to the
same party, and that is exactly the problem: with no veto between them, the
only remaining question is which office owns the restoration of the courts,
the appointments that follow it and the credit before the next presidential
election.

The Palace argues that a president elected against PiS carries the mandate for
judicial repair and must not be reduced to a signature machine. The Chancellery
argues that only a cabinet with a Sejm majority can be held responsible for
what the repair actually does to court queues, prosecutors and personnel.

Older journalists have already found the name for it. The first war at the top
was 1990, Wałęsa against Mazowiecki. The pattern being rehearsed now is the
later one: a president and a prime minister from one camp, and a president who
concludes that his own government is a liability.

[? if left_in_government: Lewica sits in that cabinet. Whatever we say about
the quarrel, we say as a governing party with ministries to lose.?][? if not
left_in_government: Lewica is outside the cabinet and can describe the quarrel
without owning either side of it.?]

- @war_top_ko_restoration
- @war_top_ko_palace_credit
- @war_top_ko_cabinet_credit
- @war_top_ko_price
- @war_top_ko_record

@war_top_ko_restoration
title: Put the repair into one bill both offices must sign in advance
subtitle: Trade credit for certainty: a written sequence of nominations, reasons and deadlines before either side briefs against the other.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: war_top_heat -= 8; war_top_palace_bloc -= 5; war_top_left_side = "institutions"; president_relation += 4; constitutional_restraint += 3; judicial_repair_mandate += 2; government_procedural_restraint += 3; news_headline = "One written sequence binds the Palace and the Chancellery before the repair begins"

Our ministers refuse to negotiate the same appointment twice. The bill fixes
who nominates, who publishes reasons and how long each stage may take, and both
offices initial it before a word of it reaches the press. Neither man gets the
photograph he wanted; judges and litigants get a procedure that survives the
quarrel.

- @poland_event_queue: Bind both offices to the sequence

@war_top_ko_palace_credit
title: Let the Palace author the repair and take the delivery
subtitle: The President signs what he wrote; the cabinet keeps the ministry and the timetable.
on-arrival: war_top_palace_bloc += 8; war_top_heat += 4; war_top_left_side = "palace"; president_relation += 8; ko_relation -= 4; government_delivery += 3; judicial_repair_mandate += 2; news_headline = "The Palace authors the judicial repair and the cabinet executes it"

We back the presidential draft, because a bill the President has written is a
bill the President cannot refuse. The repair moves. So does the Palace's
standing inside its own party, and the Chancellery notices which coalition
partner handed him the win.

- @poland_event_queue: Back the presidential draft

@war_top_ko_cabinet_credit
title: Insist that appointments belong to the responsible cabinet
subtitle: Defend the principle that a minister answerable to the Sejm makes the nominations, whoever sits in the Palace.
on-arrival: war_top_palace_bloc -= 8; war_top_heat += 5; war_top_left_side = "cabinet"; president_relation -= 6; ko_relation += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "Lewica defends cabinet responsibility against a presidential claim"

We say plainly that a president is not a second government. Appointments belong
to the minister the Sejm can dismiss, and a popular Palace is not an argument
against that. The Chancellery gains an ally; the Palace files the name of every
party that chose the losing side of a rivalry it intends to win.

- @poland_event_queue: Defend cabinet responsibility

@war_top_ko_price
title: Sell our silence for a bill of our own
subtitle: Cost: nothing now. Both offices want quiet inside the majority; make them pay in legislation rather than in goodwill.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: war_top_palace_bloc += 3; war_top_heat += 3; war_top_left_side = "price"; resources += 1; government_delivery += 2; party_unity -= 2; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Lewica names a legislative price for staying out of the KO quarrel"

We tell both offices the same thing: the Left has no view on which of them is
the real leader of the camp, and a written commitment on our own bill will keep
it that way. It works. It also teaches the coalition that our restraint is
purchasable, which is a lesson someone will use against us later.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the price and stay out

@war_top_ko_record
title: Record what the quarrel is actually about
subtitle: No side, no bargain, one published account of which office holds which power.
on-arrival: war_top_heat += 2; war_top_left_side = "undeclared"; media_capacity += 2; constitutional_restraint += 1; news_headline = "Lewica publishes an account of the powers each office actually holds"

We publish the constitutional map instead of the palace gossip: what a
president may sign, refuse, refer and nominate, and what only a cabinet with a
majority can do. Nobody thanks us. The document is still there when the quarrel
stops being about credit.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the map


@war_top_palace_alone
# prose-audit: Grade B — The Palace's first unilateral act is dated, named and
# limited to real prerogatives, and each Lewica response moves the bloc, the
# presidential relationship and legal certainty in different directions.
title: The Palace signs alone
subtitle: A prerogative exercised without the cabinet turns a rivalry into a constitutional fact
