= [+ date_label +] — Declarations

The question reaches the clubs in the crudest possible form: whose statement do
you sign. **[+ war_top_president +]**'s office circulates one; **[+ war_top_pm
+]**'s circulates another. Regional officers who have avoided the quarrel for
months discover that avoiding it is now itself an answer.

[? if war_top_split: Enough of them sign the Palace's text to make it a faction
with a name, an office and a list of people who cannot go back. That is what
happened to the last camp that tried this: a party that had governed for two
terms left a splinter behind and never recovered either half.?][? if not
war_top_split: Not enough sign to make a faction. The Palace has sympathisers,
not soldiers, and the Chancellery survives on the simple fact that it still
distributes the offices.?]

[? if war_top_camp = "lewica": For Lewica this is not spectator politics. The
people being asked to declare are our own.?][? if war_top_camp != "lewica":
Lewica watches a partner's civil war with a coalition agreement in one hand and
an election calendar in the other.?]

- @war_top_split_mediate
- @war_top_split_price
- @war_top_split_side
- @war_top_split_watch

@war_top_split_mediate
title: Convene both offices and try to hold the camp together
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. A common ticket, an agreed nomination calendar and one shared platform before the split hardens.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot finance a mediation nobody has asked for.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.war_top_heat -= 15;
Q.war_top_palace_bloc = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.war_top_palace_bloc) || 0) - 10
);
Q.war_top_left_side = "institutions";
Q.war_top_split = 0;
Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 6;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica mediates the camp's split and keeps the majority alive";
!}

We do the work nobody in the camp can do without conceding something: separate
rooms, one text, no communiqué until both sides have signed the same
nomination calendar. The faction does not form. Both men owe us a favour they
will deny owing, and the underlying question—who leads—remains unanswered.

- @poland_event_queue: Hold the camp together

@war_top_split_price
title: Name our price to whichever side wants a majority
subtitle: A splitting camp needs our votes more than it needs our opinion.
on-arrival: war_top_left_side = "price"; resources += 2; government_delivery += 2; party_unity -= 3; public_trust -= 3; war_top_heat += 5; news_headline = "Lewica prices its votes while the governing camp divides"

Both wings need 231 and neither has it alone. We take the ministries, the bill
and the list guarantees while the price is high, and we make no promise about
which leader we recognise. It is the most profitable week of the parliament and
it will be quoted back at us for years.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the price

@war_top_split_side
title: Declare for one side and help it finish the other
subtitle: Pick the winner early, and be part of what replaces the loser.
on-arrival: {!
Q.war_top_heat += 10;
if ((Number(Q.war_top_palace_bloc) || 0) >= 50) {
    Q.war_top_left_side = "palace";
    Q.war_top_palace_bloc += 10;
    Q.president_relation += 10;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 6;
    Q.news_headline = "Lewica joins the Palace bloc against the sitting cabinet";
} else {
    Q.war_top_left_side = "cabinet";
    Q.war_top_palace_bloc = Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.war_top_palace_bloc) || 0) - 12
    );
    Q.president_relation -= 10;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent -= 3;
    Q.government_delivery += 2;
    Q.news_headline = "Lewica commits to the sitting cabinet against the Palace";
}
Q.party_unity -= 2;
!}

We stop pretending to be neutral and put our weight behind the side already
winning the declarations. It shortens the fight. It also means that when the
losing side writes its account of who destroyed the camp, our name is in it.

- @poland_event_queue: Declare and commit

@war_top_split_watch
title: Refuse to save them and let the declarations run
subtitle: Keep the coalition agreement, keep our distance, and let a party discover its own arithmetic.
on-arrival: war_top_left_side = "undeclared"; war_top_heat += 6; media_capacity += 2; government_coalition_dissent += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica refuses to arbitrate a quarrel it did not start"

We honour the coalition agreement, attend the councils and answer no question
about who leads someone else's party. The split runs its course at its own
speed. Nothing is bought and nothing is owed, which is either discipline or a
missed opportunity depending on who wins.

- @poland_event_queue: Let it run


@war_top_nomination
