= [+ date_label +] — Article 154, not a dismissal

No president may dismiss a prime minister. What **[+ war_top_president +]** can
do, he has now done: he waited until **[+ war_top_pm +]** ran out of votes
inside his own camp, accepted the resignation the moment it was offered, and
nominated **[+ war_top_nominee +]** within the fourteen days the constitution
allows him.

[? if war_top_camp = "ko": Domański is the finance minister the markets and the
Commission already deal with, and the one senior figure in the party whose
standing does not depend on either man.?][? if war_top_camp = "lewica": Zawisza
carries Razem's economic programme and none of the apparatus history, which is
precisely why the machine regards the nomination as a hostile takeover of the
government.?][? if war_top_camp = "pis": Szefernaker ran the presidential
campaign. Nominating him states, without saying it, that the Palace and not the
party chairman now selects the right's prime ministers.?]

The precedent everyone cites is 2004: the same manoeuvre, a president of the
governing camp installing his own candidate, and a first confidence vote that
failed before the second one succeeded. The Sejm now has to say whether a
presidency can choose a government that the party did not choose.

- @war_top_nomination_back
- @war_top_nomination_truce
- @war_top_nomination_defend
- @war_top_nomination_abstain

@war_top_nomination_back
title: Vote for the Palace's candidate
subtitle: Confirm the nomination and negotiate our terms from inside the new cabinet.
on-arrival: war_top_left_side = "palace"; war_top_roll_base += 24; president_relation += 8; government_coalition_dissent += 4; news_headline = "Lewica votes to confirm the President's nominee"

We supply the votes and demand the portfolios in the same conversation. If the
nomination carries, the Left is a founding partner of a cabinet the Palace
built. If it fails, we have voted to remove a prime minister and failed to
replace him, which is the worst position in the chamber.

- @war_top_roll: Bring the nomination to a confidence vote

@war_top_nomination_truce
title: Offer the votes only for a caretaker who ends the dualism
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Back [+ war_top_truce_nominee +] instead: a cabinet whose mandate is the appointments statute and nothing else.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot finance the negotiation.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.war_top_nominee = Q.war_top_truce_nominee;
Q.war_top_left_side = "institutions";
Q.war_top_roll_base += 16;
Q.legal_dualism -= 4;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 5;
Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 3;
Q.court_user_trust += 2;
Q.president_relation += 3;
Q.news_headline = "Lewica trades its votes for a caretaker mandated to end the dualism";
!}

We tell the Palace that our votes are available for a government, not for a
faction. The price is the candidate: a lawyer with no leadership ambition
inside the camp, a fixed programme—the appointments statute, published reasons,
the unresolved judgments—and no claim on the 2027 lists. The Palace accepts
because the alternative is a nomination that fails.

- @war_top_roll: Bring the nomination to a confidence vote

@war_top_nomination_defend
title: Vote against and keep the incumbent
subtitle: Refuse a presidency the power to select prime ministers, whatever we think of this one.
on-arrival: war_top_left_side = "cabinet"; war_top_roll_base -= 28; president_relation -= 10; constitutional_restraint += 3; government_delivery += 1; news_headline = "Lewica votes against a prime minister chosen in the Palace"

We vote no and say why: the Sejm makes governments, and a president who
succeeds at this once will do it whenever a cabinet becomes inconvenient. The
incumbent survives or falls on other people's votes; the precedent is what we
were actually defending.

- @war_top_roll: Bring the nomination to a confidence vote

@war_top_nomination_abstain
title: Abstain and let the camp settle its own succession
subtitle: No votes, no bargain, no responsibility for either outcome.
on-arrival: war_top_left_side = "undeclared"; war_top_roll_base -= 8; media_capacity += 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Lewica abstains on the President's nominee"

We sit out a vote about who leads a party that is not ours. It is defensible
and it is also a decision: the arithmetic is now settled by people who will
remember that we were not there.

- @war_top_roll: Bring the nomination to a confidence vote

@war_top_roll
title: The confidence vote on the President's nominee
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const total = Math.max(1, Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460);
const oppositionCross = Math.round(
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 40) / 4
);
const roll = Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 9) - 4;
Q.war_top_confidence_yes = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        total,
        Math.round(Number(Q.war_top_roll_base) || 0) + oppositionCross + roll
    )
);
Q.war_top_confidence_no = Math.max(
    0,
    total - Q.war_top_confidence_yes - 12
);
Q.war_top_confidence_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    total - Q.war_top_confidence_yes - Q.war_top_confidence_no
);
Q.war_top_nomination_passed =
    Q.war_top_confidence_yes >= 231 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.war_top_nomination_passed) {
    Q.prime_minister = Q.war_top_nominee;
    Q.prime_minister_intro_return = "event_queue";
    Q.prime_minister_intro_pending = 1;
    Q.war_top_pm = Q.war_top_nominee;
    Q.government_name = Q.war_top_nominee + " cabinet";
    Q.government_has_confidence = 1;
    Q.war_top_nomination_result =
        Q.war_top_nominee + " wins confidence at the first attempt";
    Q.president_relation += 4;
    Q.government_delivery -= 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.war_top_nominee + " becomes prime minister with the President's backing";
} else {
    // Belka failed on 14 May 2004 and was confirmed on 24 June. A failed
    // first attempt is a stage in the procedure, not the end of the chain.
    Q.war_top_nomination_result =
        Q.war_top_nominee + " fails the first confidence vote";
    Q.early_election_risk += 6;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.war_top_nominee + " fails the first confidence vote and the office stays contested";
}
!}

= Recorded confidence vote

Nominee: **[+ war_top_nominee +]**

**Yes [+ war_top_confidence_yes +] · No [+ war_top_confidence_no +] · Abstain
[+ war_top_confidence_abstain +]**

[? if war_top_nomination_passed: The Sejm confirms a prime minister the Palace
selected. The camp keeps the government and loses the principle that its party,
not its president, decides who leads it.?][? if not war_top_nomination_passed:
The nomination fails. The constitution allows the chamber its own candidate and
the President a second attempt; what it does not allow is a camp with two
leaders and no cabinet indefinitely.?]

- @war_top_roll_continue: Record the vote

@war_top_roll_continue
go-to: poland_prime_minister_intro.show if war_top_nomination_passed = 1; poland_event_queue if war_top_nomination_passed = 0


@war_top_settlement
# prose-audit: Grade B — The settlement states which of the three landings
# occurred, writes it into one readable record, and hands the 2027 campaign a
# concrete inheritance rather than a mood.
title: What the war at the top left behind
subtitle: The camp counts what the quarrel cost it before the next election is called
face-image: img/poland/events/supreme-court.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 35
order: 7
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and war_top_stage >= 3 and war_top_stage < 5 and (war_top_stage = 4 or time >= war_top_started_time + 9)
on-arrival: {!
Q.war_top_stage = 5;
if (Q.war_top_nomination_passed) {
    Q.war_top_settlement =
        "Palace cabinet — " + String(Q.war_top_nominee || "the nominee") +
        " governs with the President's mandate";
    Q.legal_dualism -= 2;
    Q.president_judiciary_cooperation += 4;
    Q.government_delivery += 1;
} else if (Q.war_top_split) {
    Q.war_top_settlement =
        "Rupture — the camp enters the next election as two organisations";
    Q.public_trust -= 2;
    Q.early_election_risk += 4;
} else {
    Q.war_top_settlement =
        "Palace isolated — the prime minister survived and the new power went unused";
    Q.president_relation -= 3;
    Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
}
Q.news_headline = "The camp's war at the top is settled: " +
    Q.war_top_settlement;
!}

= [+ date_label +] — The inheritance

[? if war_top_nomination_passed: **[+ war_top_nominee +]** governs. The
presidency has demonstrated that it can select a prime minister when the camp is
weak enough, and every future cabinet of every camp will be formed in the
knowledge that this is possible.?]
[? if war_top_split and not war_top_nomination_passed: The camp goes to the
election as two organisations with one history, competing for the same voters
and blaming each other for the arithmetic. This is the part of 2004 that was
never repaired.?]
[? if not war_top_split and not war_top_nomination_passed: **[+ war_top_pm +]**
is still prime minister and **[+ war_top_president +]** still holds the
prerogatives he fought for. Nothing was resolved and nothing was destroyed; the
power sits unused, available to a president with a weaker cabinet in front of
him.?]

[? if war_top_left_side = "institutions": Lewica's record is the protocol and
the statute it insisted on, which is a thin story for a campaign and a durable
one for a state.?][? if war_top_left_side = "price": Lewica's record is what it
took while the camp was tearing itself apart. The concessions are real; so is
the reputation.?][? if war_top_left_side = "palace": Lewica's record is that it
chose the Palace, and will be asked about that whenever this presidency does
anything unpopular.?][? if war_top_left_side = "cabinet": Lewica's record is
that it defended the sitting cabinet, including the parts of it that deserved
defending less.?][? if war_top_left_side = "exploit" or war_top_left_side =
"undeclared": Lewica's record is distance: no bargain, no arbitration, no
responsibility—and no claim on what either side owes.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Close the file
